# THE DESIGN SYSTEM IS INSTALLED AS A COPY, NOT AS A LINK — and the reason is
# where `class-variance-authority` lives.
#
# `@yordan/design-system` is a `file:../../design-system` dependency, and npm's
# default for those is a symlink. Since phase R2a the package publishes React
# components as .tsx SOURCE (dist/react/*.tsx) whose first line is
#
#     import { cva, cx } from "class-variance-authority";
#
# — a peer the package deliberately does not declare, because the consumer
# brings it (see the header of any generated component). Every bundler
# canonicalises a module path before resolving that module's own imports, so
# through a symlink those files are seen at ../../design-system/dist/react/,
# and the lookup for `class-variance-authority` walks up from THERE: past
# design-system/node_modules and into the repo root's, neither of which has it
# and neither of which is this app's to change. Measured under Turbopack AND
# under webpack: three module-not-found errors, one per generated component.
#
# `install-links=true` makes npm PACK the dependency and install a real
# directory instead. Three things follow, and all three are wanted:
#
#   · resolution works, because the components' real path is now inside
#     apps/next/node_modules, where cva and react are this app's dependencies;
#   · what lands is exactly `files: [dist, css, assets]` from the package's own
#     package.json — the published surface, with the design system's tokens/,
#     components/, stories/ and scripts/ not merely unreachable by the exports
#     map but absent from the tree;
#   · `npx next build` keeps working with the default bundler, which matters
#     because .github/workflows/next.yml runs exactly that.
#
# THE COST IS STALENESS, AND IT IS NAMED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. A copy does not
# follow a design-system rebuild: after `npm run build` in design-system/, run
# `npm install` here. CI and Vercel are unaffected — both run `npm ci`, which
# re-packs from the working tree every time — so a deployed surface is never
# stale; only a local one can be, and only until the next install.
#
# A build-time freshness check comparing this copy against ../../design-system/
# dist/ was the obvious guard and is deliberately NOT here: it would put a
# literal path to another slice into scripts/sync-artifacts.mjs, which
# test/boundaries.test.js census-tests against the pinned CROSSINGS list at the
# repo root. That list is the test-engineer's file, and buying a convenience
# with an unpinned crossing is exactly what the census exists to catch. If the
# guard is wanted, the pin comes first.
install-links=true
